From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd: a definition's idle and network settings; a folder lists its tasks

Google Chrome's updater (GoogleUpdater, installed with Chrome for the
whole machine) builds its scheduled task through the object model and
asks the definition's settings for their IdleSettings to set them:
that was a stub (E_NOTIMPL), so the updater gave up and registered no
task -- Chrome never updated itself. It also lists its folder's tasks
(ITaskFolder::GetTasks, then Count and Item), which were stubs too.

Now:
- ITaskSettings::IdleSettings and NetworkSettings are objects of their
  own (settings.c: Duration, WaitTimeout, StopOnIdleEnd, RestartOnIdle;
  Name, Id), kept with the settings and written to and read from the task
  XML (IdleSettings, NetworkSettings), as is RestartOnFailure (Interval,
  Count: the settings' RestartInterval and RestartCount, which were not
  written);
- a folder's task collection has Count, Item (by 1-based index or by
  name) and _NewEnum, from the service's list (SchRpcEnumTasks; hidden
  tasks with TASK_ENUM_HIDDEN).

With these the real updater registers "GoogleUpdaterTaskSystem<version>"
(log-on and hourly calendar triggers, updater.exe --wake --system as
SYSTEM), and Run starts it (patches 1171-1173).

Test: test/taskrun-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_TASK_NO_IDLE in task.c,
SG_MUTANT_TASK_NO_LIST in regtask.c).
